tractor successfully captures some conversations but returns clean `null` for others, and make the **smallest justified implementation correction** needed to improve reliable browser conversation capture.\n\n---\n\n# 1. Verified Ground Truth\n\nKeel completed the exact existing C6 probe on 2026-09-23.\n\nEnvironment:\n\n- daemon running;\n- daemon runtime: **v2.0.21**;\n- bind: **127.0.0.1:10086**;\n- Chrome launched through the existing documented probe procedure;\n- WebBridge extension attached before capture;\n- extension remained attached throughout the test.\n\nProbe:\n\n`webbridge_extractor.py -a c6verify -s c6-probe-20260923 -m 3`\n\nResults:\n\n- process exit: **0**\n- **24/24 command calls succeeded**\n- all relevant evaluate/navigate transport calls returned `ok:true`\n- daemon telemetry showed no transport errors\n- no 502 occurred\n- C6 classification: **CONFIRMED**\n\nCapture results:\n\n- **1/3 conversations captured**\n- successful conversation:\n  - `Edge Crewise Architecture Overview`\n  - included a ~170k-character message\n  - capture artifact successfully saved\n- **2/3 conversations returned clean JavaScript `null`**\n- Keel determined those `null` results originated from the extractor's current **DOM gate**, not from daemon/extension transport failure.\n\nTherefore:\n\n> Transport is no longer the blocker.\n\nThe active problem is **extractor eligibility / DOM interpretation / capture completeness**.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Scope\n\nInspect the existing extractor implementation and the evidence from the three-chat probe.\n\nDetermine:\n\n1. What exact conditions cause the extractor to return `null`?\n2. Which DOM assumptions are encoded in the current gate?\n3. Why did the successful chat satisfy those conditions?\n4. Why did the other two conversations not satisfy them?\n5. Are the two failures caused by:\n   - selector mismatch;\n   - page-state timing;\n   - lazy rendering;\n   - conversation type/layout differences;\n   - URL/state assumptions;\n   - message-container assumptions;\n   - stale provider-specific logic;\n   - another directly evidenced condition?\n6. Is the current logic fundamentally Kimi-specific?\n7. Which portions are reusable browser-capture primitives versus provider-specific extraction logic?\n8. What is the smallest implementation change that resolves the demonstrated failure without broad redesign?\n\nFollow the evidence.\n\nDo not infer a generic browser architecture if the current defect can be corrected locally.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Evidence to Inspect\n\nUse the existing project artifacts, including where relevant:\n\n- `webbridge_extractor.py`\n- C6 probe implementation\n- Keel C6 verification evidence\n- daemon command/evaluate telemetry\n- the successful captured artifact\n- the two `null` capture cases\n- current browser DOM state for those same conversations\n- existing extractor selectors/gates\n- any provider-specific detection logic\n- existing tests\n\nKeel handoff evidence currently exists at:\n\n`C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_ORG\\02_COUNCILS\\01_Executive_Council\\Operations\\06_HANDOFFS\\Don\\20260923-KEEL-C6-WEBBRIDGE-VERIFICATION.md`\n\nCapture evidence:\n\n`...\\06_HANDOFFS\\Don\\c6-verify-2026-09-23-capture-evidence.json`\n\nTreat those as **verification evidence**, not framework canon.\n\nProject implementation truth belongs in **GCE Stack**.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Build Discipline\n\nUse:\n\n**OBSERVE → REPRODUCE → ISOLATE → CORRECT → TEST**\n\nBefore editing:\n\n- reproduce or directly inspect the `null` behavior;\n- identify the exact gate/condition responsible;\n- document the failing assumption.\n\nThen make the **smallest bounded correction**.\n\nDo not rewrite the extractor merely because a cleaner design is possible.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Required Implementation Properties\n\nAny correction must preserve:\n\n### Transport separation\nDo not alter the now-confirmed daemon ↔ extension transport contract unless direct evidence proves it necessary.\n\n### Capture ≠ interpretation