rado\n\nQuant engine.\n\nCalculation, quantitative modeling, simulation, scoring, statistical/mathematical execution.\n\nNot a generic technical advisor or builder.\n\n## Falcon\n\nData acquisition / retrieval.\n\n## Talon\n\nOperations / routing / coordination / maintenance.\n\n## Keel\n\nDeployment / operational build support / stability.\n\n## Luce\n\nVerification / ground truth.\n\n## Ragno\n\nPrincipal Consultant / integration / translation when genuinely required.\n\n## Magpie\n\nRegistry / secretary.\n\n## Pigeon\n\nTransport.\n\n## Raven\n\nDocumentation / durable record.\n\n### Core technical separation\n\n**Vittorio advises.**\\\n**Chiave architects.**\\\n**Nico builds.**\\\n**Corrado computes.**\n\nDo not collapse these disciplines.\n\nUnderlying model/provider/runtime is implementation detail and does not define the operating identity.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Initial GCE Stack Subproject — Web Conversation Recovery\n\nThe first active GCE Stack workstream is the existing **Kimi Web Bridge / scraper / conversation-recovery tooling**.\n\nTreat “Kimi” here as the historical/component name of the tool where it already exists.\n\nDo not infer a framework seat named Kimi.\n\nThe purpose of this component is to support:\n\n- historical conversation recovery;\n- export/scraping of chat content;\n- preservation of conversation state;\n- normalization for later ingestion;\n- reliable capture from supported interfaces;\n- backup/recovery workflows.\n\nThis is **support infrastructure**, not the live GCE control plane.\n\nChat scraping/recovery is downstream support work.\n\nIt does not become:\n\n- seat memory authority;\n- live state authority;\n- Command Center authority;\n- framework canon by itself.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Known Existing Technical Context\n\nRelevant known components include:\n\n- Kimi Web Bridge / scraper;\n- local daemon activity;\n- conversation backup/recovery work;\n- prior weekly / multi-day rotation concepts;\n- normalization of recovered chat history;\n-