rror; the extract() loop logs each miss explicitly (capture: skipped (wrong_path: not_chat_route pathname=...)).\n- tests/test_webbridge_extractor.py — 10 new tests (node-backed for the embedded pure JS, pythonic for the retry wrapper). 20/20 pass including all 9 existing consolidate tests.\n- README.md — two troubleshooting rows documenting the skip classifications.\nLive verification (real WebBridge browser, logged-out page)\n- captureCurrentChat() on / → {status:\"wrong_path\", reason:\"not_chat_route\"} — not null.\n- SPA redirect probe /chat/<uuid> → lands on /, extractor cleared, re-injected (exactly the loop's guard), then classifies wrong_path. This reproduced mechanism (A) live: a redirected page previously produced the silent null.\n- /chat/<uuid> → ok, /history → history_page.\nExplicit limitation\nThe required post-fix 3-chat re-probe is blocked by environment: the Default Chrome profile WebBridge drives is logged out of Kimi (0 chat links; /chat/* redirects). Final confirmation needs Don to log in, then:\n.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe src\\webbridge_extractor.py -a c6verify -s c6-probe-20260923 -m 3\nPer-chat lines will now report capture: ok or a classified skip. If all three capture → flip to EXTRACTOR COMPLETENESS CONFIRMED. If any reports wrong_path: history_page, that's a distinct route still to confirm. Stopping here per \"reward the stop\" — no further build without your word.\nRoot-cause statement: the null was produced by the pathname gate on redirected/dropped routes (A; now proven live on logout-redirect) and/or a lazy-rendered empty pane at capture (B; mitigated by retry). Neither is decidable from a logged-out session; the post-login probe settles it."]}, "create_time": 1790198441.192, "end_turn": null, "id": "f5126bb3-cc75-4abe-92a1-4acf48ec0929", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "dd77ab9b-0a43-4e8c-84f8-db361c941aa3", "turn_exchange_id": "38819c06-5311-4b27-8fbf-1cc9687b17a6", "working_turn_id": "38819c06