apture;\n- preserve prior successful artifacts when a later run fails.\n\nDo not make deletion part of this task.\n\nBackup is additive/preservative.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Safety / Non-Destructive Requirements\n\nThis scraper is read-oriented.\n\nDo not:\n\n- delete conversations;\n- archive conversations;\n- rename conversations;\n- edit messages;\n- send messages;\n- submit prompts;\n- modify account settings;\n- change ChatGPT projects;\n- manipulate memory;\n- alter browser auth/session state unnecessarily.\n\nThe browser session is a source.\n\nTreat it as read-only except for navigation/scrolling required for capture.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Authentication Boundary\n\nUse Don's current authenticated browser profile/session.\n\nDo not:\n\n- store plaintext passwords;\n- export session cookies into arbitrary files;\n- build credential replay outside the existing browser/session mechanism;\n- bypass MFA;\n- bypass access controls.\n\nIf the browser is logged out, classify the run as blocked/logged out and stop cleanly.\n\n---\n\n# 12. Browser-State Handling\n\nAccount for real SPA behavior.\n\nImplement bounded readiness handling for:\n\n- route transitions;\n- lazy rendering;\n- virtualized history;\n- message loading;\n- redirects;\n- temporary empty states.\n\nDo not use infinite waits.\n\nUse bounded retries with explicit terminal classifications.\n\n---\n\n# 13. Conversation Enumeration\n\nBuild conversation enumeration carefully.\n\nThe objective is eventually to back up the entire visible/available ChatGPT account history.\n\nDetermine how to exhaustively enumerate accessible conversations.\n\nIf the sidebar is lazy/virtualized, implement bounded controlled scrolling or another directly observed mechanism.\n\nPreserve:\n\n- conversation ID;\n- title;\n- URL;\n- discovery timestamp.\n\nDeduplicate by stable ID, not title.\n\nTitles are not unique identifiers.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Message Fidelity\n\nDo not reduce every conversation to a single plain-text blob if structured turn information is available.\n\nPreserve turn boundaries.\n\nWhere practical preserve:\n\n- role;\n- message order;\n- raw text;\n- structured blocks;\n- code;\n- links;\n- attachments/asset references;\n- citations;\n- visible metadata.\n\nIf a content type cannot yet be fully preserved, mark that explicitly in the capture metadata rather than silently dropping it.\n\n---\n\n# 15. First Milestone\n\nDo not start by scraping the entire account.\n\nThe first implementation milestone is:\n\n> **Successfully discover and back up 3 known ChatGPT conversations end-to-end using the live browser session.**\n\nSelect three conversations with materially different characteristics where practical, for example:\n\n- ordinary text conversation;\n- long conversation;\n- conversation containing code, files, citations, or other structured content.\n\nFor each one verify:\n\n- discovery;\n- navigation;\n- full capture;\n- saved artifact;\n- turn ordering;\n- no obvious truncation;\n- explicit status `ok`.\n\n---\n\n# 16. Second Milestone\n\nOnce the 3-chat proof is clean:\n\nRun a bounded larger batch.\n\nSuggested progression:\n\n- 3 chats;\n- 10 chats;\n- 25 chats;\n- then full accessible enumeration.\n\nDo not jump straight to hundreds of conversations without observing failure behavior first.\n\n---\n\n# 17. Tests\n\nAdd targeted tests for:\n\n- URL/route classification;\n- conversation ID extraction;\n- explicit error classification;\n- parsing/extraction of representative ChatGPT DOM/state;\n- incremental-state behavior;\n- retry behavior;\n- duplicate prevention;\n- serialization.\n\nDo not fake success by only unit testing mocks.\n\nLive browser verification is required.\n\n---\n\n# 18. Verification Return\n\nAt completion, return:\n\n## 1. Recon findings\nWhat you found before building.\n\n## 2. Architecture actually used\nKeep this practical and implementation-specific.\n\n## 3. Files changed/created\nExact paths.\n\n## 4. Capture source\nDOM / structured browser state / network-accessible page data / hybrid.\n\n## 5. Artifact format\nShow the resulting schema/shape.\n\n## 6. State model\nHow incremental backup works.\n\n## 7. Three-chat proof\nFor each test conversation:\n\n- ID;\n- title;\n- result;\n- message/turn count;\n- artifact path;\n- warnings.\n\n## 8. Larger batch result\nIf reached.\n\n## 9. Known limitations\nOnly observed limitations.\n\n## 10. Next smallest action\nOne action only.\n\n---\n\n# 19. Completion Classification\n\nReturn one of:\n\n### CHATGPT BACKUP MVP CONFIRMED\n\nThe system can discover, navigate, capture, persist, and re-run against ChatGPT conversations with reliable explicit state.\n\n### CHATGPT BACKUP MVP PARTIAL\n\nCore capture works but one or more explicitly identified content classes or enumeration behaviors remain incomplete.\n\n### IMPLEMENTATION DEFECT REMAINS\n\nThe current approach is reproducibly failing and needs another bounded implementation pass.\n\n### ARCHITECTURE ESCALATION REQUIRED\n\nUse only if Stage 1 or Stage 2 proves that the problem cannot reasonably be solved within the current WebBridge/provider-adapter structure.\n\nIf architecture escalation is genuinely required:\n\n- stop;\n- preserve evidence;\n- explain the exact architectural decision;\n- return to Don/Coda for possible Chiave routing.\n\nDo not self-expand into a redesign.\n\n---\n\n# 20. Project Boundary\n\nThis implementation belongs to **GCE Stack**.\n\nDo not promote project-specific implementation details into Framework canon.\n\nIf the work reveals a reusable framework-level lesson, identify it separately in the return.\n\n---\n\n# FINAL INSTRUCTION\n\nThe goal is not to build a generic scraping platform.\n\nThe goal is:\n\n> **Back up Don's ChatGPT conversations reliably from his authenticated browser session into durable local artifacts.**\n\nFirst reconstruct the current WebBridge + ChatGPT reality.\n\nThen build the smallest working ChatGPT adapter.\n\nProve it on three conversations.\n\nOnly then scale 